sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Player
    participant Client as Web or Mobile Client
    participant API as API Gateway
    participant Auth as Authentication Service
    participant Match as Matchmaking Service
    participant Redis as Redis Queue
    participant Room as Jury Room Service
    participant Case as Case Service
    participant WS as WebSocket Gateway
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Player->>Client: Login
    Client->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>Auth: Validate credentials
    Auth->>DB: Read user account
    DB-->>Auth: User details
    Auth-->>API: Access token
    API-->>Client: Login successful

    Player->>Client: Select Join Public Room
    Client->>API: POST /matchmaking/join
    API->>Match: Add authenticated user
    Match->>Redis: Add player to waiting queue
    Redis-->>Match: Queue position

    alt Fewer than six players available
        Match-->>Client: Waiting for players
    else Six players available
        Match->>Redis: Atomically reserve six players
        Match->>Room: Create jury room
        Room->>DB: Store room and participants
        DB-->>Room: Room created

        Room->>Case: Request eligible case
        Case->>DB: Fetch unpublished case for players
        DB-->>Case: Case information
        Case-->>Room: Selected case

        Room->>Redis: Save active room state
        Room-->>Match: Room ready
        Match-->>Client: Match found with room ID

        Client->>WS: Connect using room token
        WS->>Room: Register player connection
        Room->>Redis: Mark player connected
        Room-->>WS: Current room state
        WS-->>Client: Case reading phase started

        Room-->>WS: Publish case summary and evidence
        WS-->>Client: Display case material

        Note over Player,Room: All six players read the case

        Room-->>WS: Start initial voting phase
        WS-->>Client: Request private initial vote
        Player->>Client: Submit initial opinion
        Client->>WS: Initial vote
        WS->>Room: Store initial vote
        Room->>DB: Persist initial vote

        Room-->>WS: Start discussion phase
        WS-->>Client: Enable jury discussion

        loop During deliberation
            Player->>Client: Send message or speak
            Client->>WS: Discussion event
            WS->>Room: Validate room and phase
            Room-->>WS: Broadcast event
            WS-->>Client: Show discussion update
        end

        Room-->>WS: Discussion time completed
        WS-->>Client: Start final voting phase
    end